WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
Storylines, Level 1.

00:09.000 --> 00:12.000
The Watchers by Jennifer Bassett.

00:18.000 --> 00:20.950
1. The big caves.

00:21.000 --> 00:25.000
Storylines, Level 2. The big caves.

00:52.000 --> 00:54.950
Are we dead or alive?

00:55.000 --> 00:56.950
It is not important.

00:57.000 --> 01:00.950
We sit and we wait and we watch.

01:01.000 --> 01:03.950
For 3,000 years.

01:04.000 --> 01:07.950
We are the Watchers.

01:08.000 --> 01:09.950
The guard is here too.

01:10.000 --> 01:11.950
The guard to Poseidon.

01:12.000 --> 01:14.950
The guard of the sea stands here in this fall.

01:15.000 --> 01:16.950
We watch his statue.

01:17.000 --> 01:18.950
It is gold.

01:19.000 --> 01:20.950
All gold.

01:21.000 --> 01:23.950
He stands here 5 meters tall.

01:24.000 --> 01:25.950
His arms are gold.

01:26.000 --> 01:27.950
His hair is gold.

01:28.000 --> 01:29.950
His face is gold.

01:30.000 --> 01:32.950
And his gold eyes shine.

01:33.000 --> 01:34.950
His dark fall.

01:35.000 --> 01:37.950
We are the Watchers.

01:38.000 --> 01:41.950
Jim and Stella, his sister, are on holiday in Greece.

01:42.000 --> 01:45.950
They are staying at a hotel in Iraqlion, on Crete.

01:46.000 --> 01:48.950
They are talking to their friend, Nikos.

01:49.000 --> 01:54.000
Nikos is a Cretean and lives near the Palace of Knosses.

02:02.000 --> 02:03.950
What are we going to do tomorrow?

02:04.000 --> 02:05.950
Can we go to Knosses?

02:06.000 --> 02:06.950
Yes.

02:07.000 --> 02:07.950
Why not?

02:08.000 --> 02:09.950
It is a very famous place.

02:10.000 --> 02:11.950
And very, very old.

02:12.000 --> 02:14.950
About 3,000 or 4,000 years old.

02:15.000 --> 02:16.950
Yes, I would like to.

02:17.000 --> 02:18.950
Stella, look at this.

02:19.000 --> 02:19.950
It is about Knosses.

02:20.000 --> 02:21.950
It is very interesting.

02:22.000 --> 02:23.950
Caves under Knosses.

02:24.000 --> 02:25.950
Iraqlion, Crete.

02:26.000 --> 02:29.950
Under the famous Palace of Knosses, there are many caves.

02:30.000 --> 02:32.950
Some of these caves are very big.

02:33.000 --> 02:35.950
There are many, many meters under the ground.

02:36.000 --> 02:37.950
What is in these caves?

02:38.000 --> 02:38.950
Nobody knows.

02:39.000 --> 02:41.950
The caves are very dangerous.

02:42.000 --> 02:45.950
Next week, Janis Padakis is going to...

02:46.000 --> 02:48.950
We are going to find these caves, Stella.

02:49.000 --> 02:50.950
Are you coming with us, Nikos?

02:51.000 --> 02:51.950
But Jim?

02:52.000 --> 02:52.950
Yes, yes.

02:53.000 --> 02:53.950
I am coming with you.

02:54.000 --> 02:57.950
You can stay with me at my mother's house near Knosses.

02:58.000 --> 02:58.950
Good.

02:59.000 --> 03:00.950
We are going to need a lot of things.

03:01.000 --> 03:03.950
We are going to find the caves under Knosses.

03:04.000 --> 03:05.950
Yes, but it is OK.

03:06.000 --> 03:07.950
I can get everything.

03:08.000 --> 03:10.950
Jim, the caves are dangerous.

03:11.000 --> 03:13.950
Yes, but Nikos knows a lot about caves.

03:14.000 --> 03:14.950
Yes, I do.

03:15.000 --> 03:17.950
And I know the Palace of Knosses very well.

03:18.000 --> 03:19.950
Don't forget, I won't there.

03:20.000 --> 03:22.950
But do you know these caves under Knosses?

03:23.000 --> 03:24.950
No, I don't.

03:25.000 --> 03:26.950
But we are going to be careful.

03:27.000 --> 03:27.950
Oh, all right.

03:28.000 --> 03:29.950
When are we going?

03:30.000 --> 03:36.950
Tomorrow.

03:37.000 --> 03:40.950
Sometimes the Relights in these halls are music.

03:41.000 --> 03:43.950
The people from the Palace come down here.

03:44.000 --> 03:47.950
They are small, quick people with dark eyes and dark hair.

03:48.000 --> 03:51.950
They bring lights and food and water.

03:52.000 --> 03:54.950
And they dance the dance of the God.

03:55.000 --> 03:58.000
They are the Gods people.

03:59.000 --> 04:01.950
No, no, I forget.

04:02.000 --> 04:03.950
They do not come now.

04:04.000 --> 04:08.950
These halls are quiet, dark and quiet.

04:09.000 --> 04:10.950
It is always night now.

04:11.000 --> 04:14.950
There is no music, no dancing.

04:15.000 --> 04:17.950
There are no people in the Palace now.

04:18.000 --> 04:20.950
Not after the fire and the water from the sea.

04:21.000 --> 04:24.950
They are dead, all dead.

04:25.000 --> 04:28.950
And we, the Ketter and I, sit in the hall of the God.

04:29.000 --> 04:31.950
We wait and we watch.

04:32.000 --> 04:36.000
We are the Gods watches.

04:44.000 --> 04:45.950
Two.

04:46.000 --> 04:47.950
The first day.

04:48.000 --> 04:49.950
At the Palace of Knosses.

04:50.000 --> 04:52.950
It is seven o'clock in the morning.

04:53.000 --> 04:55.950
Knickers is looking for the door to the caves.

04:56.000 --> 04:58.950
Jim and Stella are waiting for him.

04:59.000 --> 05:01.950
The sun is hot.

05:02.000 --> 05:04.950
I'm thirsty. I'm going to drink some water.

05:05.000 --> 05:07.950
Don't drink a lot. We need it in the caves.

05:08.000 --> 05:09.950
Have we got everything?

05:10.000 --> 05:12.950
I think so. The bags are very heavy.

05:13.000 --> 05:15.950
Jim, Stella, the door is here.

05:16.000 --> 05:19.000
Come on. We can go down now.

05:24.000 --> 05:25.950
Be careful.

05:26.000 --> 05:27.950
It's very dark.

05:28.000 --> 05:29.950
I can't see anything.

05:30.000 --> 05:31.950
Here. Hold this light.

05:32.000 --> 05:33.950
We need all the lights now.

05:34.000 --> 05:36.950
Walk slowly and be very careful.

05:37.000 --> 05:39.950
Yes, I know.

05:40.000 --> 05:42.950
How many caves are there?

05:43.000 --> 05:44.950
This is the 10th cave now.

05:45.000 --> 05:47.950
I can see another one in front of us.

05:48.000 --> 05:50.000
A long one.

05:51.000 --> 05:52.950
I'm tired.

05:53.000 --> 05:55.950
I don't want to look at any more caves today.

05:56.000 --> 05:58.950
How about some food? I'm hungry.

05:59.000 --> 06:00.950
Yes. Let's eat something.

06:01.000 --> 06:02.950
And we can stay here for the night.

06:03.000 --> 06:06.950
Good. Where's the bag? The food is in there.

06:07.000 --> 06:08.950
How old are these caves, Nikos?

06:09.000 --> 06:10.950
I don't know.

06:11.000 --> 06:13.950
3,000 years? 4,000 years?

06:14.000 --> 06:17.000
Do many people come to these caves?

06:18.000 --> 06:19.950
Not many people know.

06:20.000 --> 06:22.950
Only the old Greek gods.

06:23.000 --> 06:25.950
The god Poseidon lives in caves.

06:26.000 --> 06:28.950
Some people say that God Poseidon.

06:29.000 --> 06:30.950
There are no old gods in these caves.

06:31.000 --> 06:32.950
How do you know, Jim?

06:33.000 --> 06:35.950
The old Greek gods are only stories.

06:36.000 --> 06:37.950
We read about them in books.

06:38.000 --> 06:39.950
They're not important today.

06:40.000 --> 06:40.950
Oh, yes, they are.

06:41.000 --> 06:42.950
Don't laugh at them.

06:43.000 --> 06:44.950
And Poseidon is a dangerous god.

06:45.000 --> 06:46.950
All the books say that.

06:47.000 --> 06:48.950
He's the god of the sea.

06:49.000 --> 06:50.950
And the god of earthquakes too.

06:51.000 --> 06:53.950
We have a lot of earthquakes in Greece.

06:54.000 --> 06:54.950
Don't forget that.

06:55.000 --> 06:56.950
Oh, Nikos.

06:57.000 --> 06:57.950
That's silly.

06:58.000 --> 06:59.950
The god of earthquakes.

07:00.000 --> 07:01.950
Everybody knows the earthquakes.

07:02.000 --> 07:02.950
No, Jim.

07:03.000 --> 07:04.950
Nikos is right.

07:05.000 --> 07:06.950
We don't understand everything.

07:07.000 --> 07:08.950
And don't laugh at Poseidon.

07:09.000 --> 07:11.000
Not here in these caves.

07:15.000 --> 07:18.950
The years come and the years go.

07:19.000 --> 07:21.950
3,000 years.

07:22.000 --> 07:25.950
My sister, Aketa, and I sit and wait.

07:26.000 --> 07:29.950
It is dark and cold in the hall of the god.

07:30.000 --> 07:32.950
The sun never shines here.

07:33.000 --> 07:35.950
Sometimes people come to these halls.

07:36.000 --> 07:37.950
They are not the god's people.

07:38.000 --> 07:39.950
They look for gold.

07:40.000 --> 07:41.950
Only gold.

07:42.000 --> 07:43.950
And Poseidon is angry.

07:44.000 --> 07:46.950
It is the gold of his people.

07:47.000 --> 07:51.950
And now it is the god's gold because his people are dead.

07:52.000 --> 07:58.950
Nobody can take the god's gold or look at the gold face of the god and live.

07:59.000 --> 08:00.950
But there are no lights.

08:01.000 --> 08:02.950
No people now.

08:03.000 --> 08:06.950
Only the god Poseidon stands here in this dark hall.

08:07.000 --> 08:08.950
God of the blue sea.

08:09.000 --> 08:10.950
God of the green sea.

08:11.000 --> 08:13.950
God of this dark hall.

08:14.000 --> 08:19.000
We are his watchers.

08:20.000 --> 08:45.950
3, the second day.

08:46.000 --> 08:47.950
Wake up, Stella.

08:48.000 --> 08:49.950
Good morning, Nickos.

08:50.000 --> 08:50.950
Morning.

08:51.000 --> 08:52.950
It is always night in these caves.

08:53.000 --> 08:54.950
What is the time?

08:55.000 --> 08:55.950
7 o'clock.

08:56.000 --> 08:57.950
Are we going on or back?

08:58.000 --> 08:59.950
What do you think, Nickos?

09:00.000 --> 09:01.950
I don't know.

09:02.000 --> 09:03.950
How many caves are there?

09:04.000 --> 09:05.950
15, 20?

09:06.000 --> 09:06.950
I don't know.

09:07.000 --> 09:08.950
But we can look at the next one.

09:09.000 --> 09:09.950
Or two.

09:10.000 --> 09:12.950
Or three, or four, or five.

09:13.000 --> 09:13.950
I know you, Jim.

09:14.000 --> 09:16.000
You want to see everything.

09:17.000 --> 09:19.950
This is the 14th cave.

09:20.000 --> 09:21.950
And this cave is big.

09:22.000 --> 09:22.950
Very big.

09:23.000 --> 09:23.950
Look.

09:24.000 --> 09:25.950
This is a road.

09:26.000 --> 09:27.950
We're walking on a road.

09:28.000 --> 09:28.950
Yes.

09:29.000 --> 09:29.950
You're right.

09:30.000 --> 09:31.950
It's a very old road too.

09:32.000 --> 09:34.950
Look at these stones on the floor.

09:35.000 --> 09:36.950
Thousands of years old.

09:37.000 --> 09:38.950
But whose road is it?

09:39.000 --> 09:40.950
And where does it go to?

09:41.000 --> 09:41.950
I don't know.

09:42.000 --> 09:43.950
But we can follow it.

09:44.000 --> 09:45.950
But it's six o'clock now.

09:46.000 --> 09:47.950
I think...

09:48.000 --> 09:48.950
Listen.

09:49.000 --> 09:49.950
I can hear water.

09:50.000 --> 09:51.950
Can you hear it?

09:52.000 --> 09:53.950
There's a river in front of us.

09:54.000 --> 09:55.950
We can't get across a river.

09:56.000 --> 09:57.950
Oh, yes, we can.

09:58.000 --> 09:59.950
I don't want to go across.

10:00.000 --> 10:00.950
It's dangerous.

10:01.000 --> 10:01.950
No, it isn't.

10:02.000 --> 10:03.950
Come on, Stella.

10:04.000 --> 10:05.950
Stella's right.

10:06.000 --> 10:07.950
Rivers under the ground are dangerous.

10:08.000 --> 10:09.950
Listen.

10:10.000 --> 10:11.950
I can hear something.

10:12.000 --> 10:13.950
It's only the river, Stella.

10:14.000 --> 10:15.950
It's all right.

10:16.000 --> 10:17.950
We can go across the river.

10:18.000 --> 10:20.950
And then we can stop and stay there for the night.

10:21.000 --> 10:21.950
Yes.

10:22.000 --> 10:25.000
We can make a fire and have some food.

10:31.000 --> 10:32.950
Listen, Sister.

10:33.000 --> 10:34.950
Do you hear anything?

10:35.000 --> 10:36.950
There are people at the river.

10:37.000 --> 10:38.950
They are talking and laughing.

10:39.000 --> 10:40.950
Listen, Sister.

10:41.000 --> 10:44.950
They are coming here to the hall of the God.

10:45.000 --> 10:46.950
Why?

10:47.000 --> 10:48.950
Who are they?

10:49.000 --> 10:50.950
What do they want?

10:51.000 --> 10:52.950
Gold.

10:53.000 --> 10:54.950
They want gold.

10:55.000 --> 10:56.950
All people want gold.

10:57.000 --> 10:58.950
They cannot eat it.

10:59.000 --> 11:00.950
They cannot drink it.

11:01.000 --> 11:06.000
But the love of gold is in all men and women too.

11:07.000 --> 11:09.950
But they cannot take the God's gold.

11:10.000 --> 11:11.950
We are His watchers.

11:12.000 --> 11:15.950
We call the God and we say His name.

11:16.000 --> 11:21.000
Then the God wakes and His speaks.

11:31.000 --> 11:31.950
Gold.

11:32.000 --> 11:34.000
The third day.

11:37.000 --> 11:39.950
When are we going to go back?

11:40.000 --> 11:41.950
This is the third day now.

11:42.000 --> 11:43.950
I don't like these caves.

11:44.000 --> 11:45.950
Why not, Stella?

11:46.000 --> 11:47.950
I don't know.

11:48.000 --> 11:49.950
I can hear something.

11:50.000 --> 11:51.950
Or someone.

11:52.000 --> 11:53.950
It's not the river.

11:54.000 --> 11:55.950
I want to go back, Nikos.

11:56.000 --> 11:56.950
Yes.

11:57.000 --> 11:59.950
Sometimes I can hear something too.

12:00.000 --> 12:02.950
But there's nobody in these caves, Stella.

12:03.000 --> 12:04.000
Only us.

12:05.000 --> 12:06.950
Let's look at one more cave.

12:07.000 --> 12:08.950
Then we can go back.

12:09.000 --> 12:09.950
Okay?

12:10.000 --> 12:11.950
What's Jim doing?

12:12.000 --> 12:12.950
I don't know.

12:13.000 --> 12:14.950
He's looking at something.

12:15.000 --> 12:16.950
Jim, what are you...

12:17.000 --> 12:17.950
Hey, look at this.

12:18.000 --> 12:18.950
It's a bowl.

12:19.000 --> 12:20.950
A gold bowl.

12:21.000 --> 12:22.950
It's beautiful.

12:23.000 --> 12:24.950
Can I hold it for a minute?

12:25.000 --> 12:26.950
It's very heavy too.

12:27.000 --> 12:28.950
Look at all this gold.

12:29.000 --> 12:29.950
Is it old, Nikos?

12:30.000 --> 12:30.950
Yes.

12:31.000 --> 12:32.950
Thousands of years old, I think.

12:33.000 --> 12:34.950
We can sell it.

12:35.000 --> 12:36.950
We can get a lot of money for this bowl.

12:37.000 --> 12:37.950
We can't do that.

12:38.000 --> 12:38.950
It's not ours.

12:39.000 --> 12:39.950
Who's is it, then?

12:40.000 --> 12:41.950
It's, well, it's...

12:42.000 --> 12:43.950
I don't know.

12:44.000 --> 12:44.950
But it's not ours.

12:45.000 --> 12:46.950
Don't take it, Jim.

12:47.000 --> 12:47.950
Leave it here.

12:48.000 --> 12:48.950
No.

12:49.000 --> 12:49.950
I'm going to take it.

12:50.000 --> 12:51.950
It's ours now.

12:52.000 --> 12:53.950
Can you hear them, sister?

12:54.000 --> 12:55.950
They are near the hall now.

12:56.000 --> 12:57.950
Listen.

12:58.000 --> 13:00.950
They are looking for gold.

13:01.000 --> 13:01.950
Gold.

13:02.000 --> 13:05.000
All people want gold.

13:09.000 --> 13:10.950
Look at that next cave.

13:11.000 --> 13:11.950
Can you see it?

13:12.000 --> 13:13.950
It's huge.

13:14.000 --> 13:14.950
It's not a cave.

13:15.000 --> 13:15.950
It's a...

13:16.000 --> 13:16.950
A hole.

13:17.000 --> 13:17.950
A huge hole.

13:18.000 --> 13:19.950
Jim, Nikos, don't go in there.

13:20.000 --> 13:21.950
Why not, Stella?

13:22.000 --> 13:23.950
I think someone is watching us.

13:24.000 --> 13:25.950
I don't like it.

13:26.000 --> 13:28.950
Why don't we go back, please?

13:29.000 --> 13:30.950
Who is watching us?

13:31.000 --> 13:32.950
We're the only people here.

13:33.000 --> 13:33.950
I don't know.

13:34.000 --> 13:37.950
But someone or something is watching us.

13:38.000 --> 13:38.950
And it doesn't like us.

13:39.000 --> 13:40.950
Don't be silly, Stella.

13:41.000 --> 13:42.950
Nothing is watching us.

13:43.000 --> 13:44.000
Come on.

13:47.000 --> 13:49.950
I can see them now, sister.

13:50.000 --> 13:51.950
Two men and a woman.

13:52.000 --> 13:52.950
They are young.

13:53.000 --> 13:55.950
Two of them have blue eyes.

13:56.000 --> 13:57.950
They are not people from the palace.

13:58.000 --> 14:01.000
They are not the gods, people.

14:03.000 --> 14:04.950
And they cannot come in here.

14:05.000 --> 14:07.950
They cannot take the gods gold.

14:08.000 --> 14:13.000
They cannot look at the face of the god.

14:17.000 --> 14:18.950
Look at those statues there.

14:19.000 --> 14:20.950
They're very, very old.

14:21.000 --> 14:22.950
I don't like them.

14:23.000 --> 14:24.950
Look at their eyes.

14:25.000 --> 14:27.000
Come away, Stella.

14:28.000 --> 14:29.950
I can see something at the end of the whole.

14:30.000 --> 14:30.950
Look.

14:31.000 --> 14:31.950
What is it?

14:32.000 --> 14:33.950
It's tall.

14:34.000 --> 14:35.950
Very tall.

14:36.000 --> 14:38.950
It's a statue, a huge statue.

14:39.000 --> 14:40.950
And it's shining.

14:41.000 --> 14:42.950
It's gold.

14:43.000 --> 14:44.950
Oh, gold.

14:45.000 --> 14:46.950
Don't look at it.

14:47.000 --> 14:47.950
Don't go in there.

14:48.000 --> 14:48.950
Please, Jim.

14:49.000 --> 14:49.950
Please.

14:50.000 --> 14:50.950
It's dangerous.

14:51.000 --> 14:51.950
Stop him, Nick.

14:52.000 --> 14:53.950
Stop him.

14:54.000 --> 14:56.950
They are looking into the whole now.

14:57.000 --> 14:58.950
Call the god.

14:59.000 --> 15:00.950
Now, sister.

15:01.000 --> 15:01.950
Now.

15:02.000 --> 15:04.950
Say the name of the god.

15:05.000 --> 15:06.950
They cannot come in.

15:07.000 --> 15:10.000
They cannot come in.

15:13.000 --> 15:13.950
Be quiet for a minute.

15:14.000 --> 15:15.950
Wait, Jim.

15:16.000 --> 15:16.950
Listen.

15:17.000 --> 15:17.950
Why?

15:18.000 --> 15:18.950
What's...

15:19.000 --> 15:20.950
I think Stella's right.

15:21.000 --> 15:21.950
There's something...

15:22.000 --> 15:22.950
Listen.

15:23.000 --> 15:23.950
Because...

15:24.000 --> 15:25.950
What's that?

15:26.000 --> 15:26.950
Can you hear it?

15:27.000 --> 15:27.950
Oh, no.

15:28.000 --> 15:28.950
No.

15:29.000 --> 15:29.950
The ground is moving.

15:30.000 --> 15:31.950
It's an earthquake.

15:32.000 --> 15:33.950
There's going to be an earthquake.

15:34.000 --> 15:34.950
The stones are falling.

15:35.000 --> 15:35.950
Run.

15:36.000 --> 15:36.950
Run.

15:37.000 --> 15:37.950
Back to the river.

15:38.000 --> 15:38.950
Run.

15:39.000 --> 15:39.950
Quick, Stella.

15:40.000 --> 15:40.950
Run.

15:41.000 --> 15:41.950
Run.

15:42.000 --> 15:42.950
We can't.

15:43.000 --> 15:44.950
The walls are falling.

15:45.000 --> 15:45.950
Everything is falling.

15:46.000 --> 15:47.950
We can't get out.

15:48.000 --> 15:50.000
We can't get out.

15:57.000 --> 15:58.950
Creek News.

15:59.000 --> 16:00.950
14th of August.

16:01.000 --> 16:03.950
Earthquake at Knosses.

16:04.000 --> 16:06.950
Three young people are dead.

16:07.000 --> 16:09.950
Erachlion Creek.

